course: dictionary
lesson: 10749
title: Urdu and words that travelled
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Urdu is a language. It is spoken mainly in Pakistan and India, and many families in the UK, the USA and Canada speak it at home too. Urdu is the national language of Pakistan.
explain: Urdu is written with an Arabic-style script, and you read it from right to left. When spoken, it sounds very close to Hindi, but the writing looks different. Urdu can also be an adjective: «Urdu poetry» is poetry that belongs to the Urdu language.
explain: Look at the clues in this sentence: «Priya's grandma in Leicester smiles: "Pyjamas, shampoo and bungalow are Hindi words, beta!"» Beta is a loving word for a child, and the smile tells you Grandma is pleased. Words can travel between languages, and English has many from Hindi and Urdu.
fact: Urdu is spoken mainly in Pakistan and India.
fact: Urdu is written from right to left, in an Arabic-style script.
fact: «Pyjamas», «shampoo» and «bungalow» came from Hindi and Urdu during British rule in India.
fact: «Beta» is a loving word for a child in Hindi and Urdu.
fact: «Yaar» means mate in Hindi and Urdu.
exercise: Which language is written from right to left in an Arabic-style script? | *Urdu | Welsh | Hindi | English
exercise: Priya's grandma calls her «beta». What does beta mean? | A word for grumpy | *A loving word for a child | A kind of bread | A petrol station
exercise: In «Urdu poetry», what kind of word is Urdu? | A country | A verb | *An adjective | A noun
test: Which two countries mainly speak Urdu? | *Pakistan and India | France and Spain | Egypt and Greece | Japan and China
test: When spoken, Urdu sounds very close to which language? | Welsh | Greek | *Hindi | Italian
exam: Which statement about Urdu is true? | It is written from left to right | It is a kind of food | It is spoken only in the UK | *It is written from right to left
